Subject: [PATCH 8/8] sbrdecoder: a USAC channel pair's second channel gets the SBR mode from the first header

VibeSDR patch for libxaac v0.1.14 (commit 2fbadd57; the decoder VibeServer links for xHE-AAC). Apache-2.0, as libxaac.
Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-29; applied in the order of xaac-patches/series by vibeserver/linux/build-libxaac.sh (Linux
and Mac). Every file it changes carries a "Modified by VibeSDR" notice (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). Measured with
xaacbench on the 7 ISO conformance streams, 12 xHE test streams (usac/xhe) and 4 off-air DAB+ unit logs, at PCM16 as
the server decodes, on arm64, armhf, ARMv6, i386 and amd64 (qemu) and the Mac. Instruction counts: qemu, guest
instructions per second of audio.

DEFECT FIX. On a USAC SBR header in a CPE only frame_data[0]->sbr_mode was set; frame_data[1] stayed UNKNOWN_SBR
until the end of the first frame. The right channel's first frame therefore skipped the HF adjustment, and its
noise/sine phase index (f_IndexNoise) ran exactly one frame (832 steps) behind the left for the rest of the stream.
Right channel against macOS AudioToolbox on fd_st32_sbr: median 24 dB before, 76.5 dB after (the left was and is
76.5); the SBR bands 5-12 kHz went from ~10 dB to ~72 dB. AudioToolbox was right. Changes only the right channel of
stereo-SBR USAC streams (here fd_st32_sbr, fd_st32_harm, sw_st20_ites).

diff --git a/decoder/ixheaacd_sbrdecoder.c b/decoder/ixheaacd_sbrdecoder.c
index 3db98fd..fec6ad6 100644
--- a/decoder/ixheaacd_sbrdecoder.c
+++ b/decoder/ixheaacd_sbrdecoder.c
@@ -16,6 +16,12 @@
  *
  *****************************************************************************
  * Originally developed and contributed by Ittiam Systems Pvt. Ltd, Bangalore
+ *
+ * Modified by VibeSDR, 2026-10-29: when a USAC SBR header arrives in a channel
+ * pair element, the second channel's frame data takes the SBR mode too. It was
+ * left unset (UNKNOWN_SBR) until the end of the first frame, so the right
+ * channel's first frame got no HF adjustment and its noise/phase index ran one
+ * frame behind the left for the rest of the stream.
 */
 #include <string.h>
 #include "ixheaacd_sbr_common.h"
@@ -527,6 +533,8 @@ IA_ERRORCODE ixheaacd_applysbr(
               } else {
                 ptr_frame_data[k]->sbr_mode = PVC_SBR;
               }
+              /* VibeSDR: a channel pair's second channel takes the same mode */
+              if (stereo) ptr_frame_data[1]->sbr_mode = ptr_frame_data[k]->sbr_mode;
             }
             if (header_flag == SBR_RESET) {
               err = ixheaacd_calc_frq_bnd_tbls(ptr_header_data[k],
@@ -571,6 +579,8 @@ IA_ERRORCODE ixheaacd_applysbr(
               } else {
                 ptr_frame_data[k]->sbr_mode = PVC_SBR;
               }
+              /* VibeSDR: a channel pair's second channel takes the same mode */
+              if (stereo) ptr_frame_data[1]->sbr_mode = ptr_frame_data[k]->sbr_mode;
             }
 
